| GiveBack: every frame given back to RISC OS (hevcdec_frame_free) as soon
| as no picture to come refers to it, before the next picture is given to
| the block, as FFmpeg's hevc_hwdec now does with its spare ones. The
| picture before may still be reading it: hevcdec frees it once the block
| is past. Pipelined (-p -G), every picture checked, 1080p and 4K. Each
| run says how many frames were given back. Reports to ResultG.
| (a GCCSDK program: needs SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport loaded)
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error This needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error This needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
WimpSlot -min 98304K -max 98304K
Remove <Obey$Dir>.ResultG
Run <Obey$Dir>.hevctest -p -G -o <Obey$Dir>.ResultG <Obey$Dir>.clips.small.trace
Run <Obey$Dir>.hevctest -p -G -o <Obey$Dir>.ResultG <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd.trace
Run <Obey$Dir>.hevctest -p -G -o <Obey$Dir>.ResultG <Obey$Dir>.clips.hd10.trace
Run <Obey$Dir>.hevctest -p -G -f 10 -o <Obey$Dir>.ResultG <Obey$Dir>.clips.uhd.trace
Run <Obey$Dir>.hevctest -p -G -f 10 -o <Obey$Dir>.ResultG <Obey$Dir>.clips.uhd10.trace
